-- title:
--   Original BV strictly precontact stopped-grid positive C1 Taylor error vanishes in mean
-- statement:
--   The actual BV Lévy process, admissible dividend strategy and stopped physical grid have positive Taylor-error mean tending to zero on the strict precontact prefix k-1. Starting from the full grid's endpoint and monotonicity, prove the strict prefix is a valid stopped grid. The final ruin/horizon contact cell is deliberately excluded from the compact C1 assumptions.
-- source:
--   Apply the independently Proved strict-grid geometry to k-1, transfer measurability of the original random stopping index and its bounded envelope, then instantiate the accepted genuine-original-process Taylor positive-error L1 convergence theorem. This avoids circular BV prebudget assumptions and avoids imposing smoothness at the final ruin/cap contact cell.

